## 5. Your keys, licenses and data

License Generator stores your signing keys, license history and settings on your
device and transmits nothing to the Licensor. See the **Privacy Policy**.

Private keys, history and backups are stored **without encryption**. You are
responsible for keeping them private and for your own backups. The Licensor
holds no copy of your keys or licenses and cannot recover them. If you lose a
private key, you cannot issue licenses that applications already distributed
with its public key will accept. If a private key leaks, anyone holding it can
issue licenses for those applications.

## 6. What offline licenses do not do

A license issued by License Generator is a signed statement that your
application verifies on the user's device without contacting a server. A
signature shows that the license was issued with your key and has not been
altered. It cannot stop a user who controls a device from modifying your
application or its clock, it cannot be revoked remotely, and hardware binding
and expiration are only as strong as the checks your application performs. How
well your software is protected depends on your own client implementation.

